                <pb facs="0580" n="1234" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1234"/>

                <head>No. 6.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Comyn
                        to the Earl of Derby.—(Received December</hi>
                    16.)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 14,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: In conformity with the orders received
                    from my government, I have the honor of inclosing herewith a check drawn with
                    this day’s date upon Messrs. Frederick Huth &amp; Co., of this city, to the
                    order of your excellency as principal secretary of state for foreign affairs,
                    for the sum of £6,700 sterling, agreed upon for the settlement of the affair of
                    the steamer Virginius.</p>
                <p>I beg that your excellency will be pleased to acknowledge the receipt of the said
                    sum.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JUAN S. COMYN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
